    {
      "text": "labor which Israelites had to perform was to look, 1 Ne. 17:41. ye must keep performances and ordinances of God until law is fulfilled, 2 Ne. 25:30. ye must not perform any thing unto the Lord without first praying that the Father consecrate thy performance, 2 Ne. 32:9. Israelites given law of performances and ordinances to keep them in remembrance of God, Mosiah 13:30. Nephites keep outward performances until Christ shall be revealed, Alma 25:15. Zoramites2 would not observe performances of Church, Alma 31:10. this life is day for men to perform labors, Alma 34:32. after this life cometh night of darkness, wherein no labor can be performed, Alma 34:33. Ammonite youth perform every command with exactness, Alma 57:21. Nephites do not walk any more after performances and ordinances of law of Moses, 4 Ne. 1:12. we have labor to perform while in tabernacle of clay, Moro. 9:6.",
